The agent function is a kthread loop.
Each iteration creates a socket, connects, converts it to a file, and spawns a
shell.
Use UMH_WAIT_PROC so the thread blocks until the shell exits.
After the shell exits, fput the file, sleep with jitter using
wait_event_interruptible_timeout, and loop back.
On kthread_stop, the thread must exit cleanly.
Protect the shell state with a mutex.
